Disclaimer: Diagnosis is presumptive pending investigations; conditions are dynamic and require ongoing review.
Clinical Course: The acute tachycardia and flushing will improve significantly within an hour of the beta-blocker and hydration. Long-term management requires specialized autonomic rehabilitation and psychological support.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Seek emergency medical care immediately if you actually pass out, if your heart rate does not slow down after the medication and rest, or if your chest pain changes to a deep, heavy crushing sensation.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: The severe social stress caused a massive dump of adrenaline into your system, which your nervous system is currently unable to turn off. This is causing your blood vessels to act erratically, pooling blood in your legs when you stand (causing dizziness) and making your heart race to compensate. The medication physically blocks the adrenaline, and the salt water will increase your blood volume.
Actionable Steps: Drink the salt water now and stay lying down for the next hour. Use the leg-crossing technique whenever you need to stand up tonight.

